WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.300
A child process can inherit environment variables from the parent, and those variables can influence runtime behavior.

2
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:15.880
They may affect configuration lookup, locale, temporary directory selection, logging, library behavior, proxy settings, and other assumptions.

3
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:20.220
The parent should decide which environment is appropriate for the child.

4
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:26.580
A minimal or controlled environment is often easier to review than inheriting everything.

5
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.640
Some tools need a specific set of variables.

6
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.540
Others can run with a deliberately small environment.

7
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:38.320
The code should build that environment intentionally where practical and document why inherited values are allowed.

8
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:45.480
Locale and encoding-related environment values can change parsing, comparison, formatting, and diagnostics.

9
00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:49.660
Temporary directory variables can influence where files are created.

10
00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:55.200
Configuration-related variables can change which files or services a helper uses.

11
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.460
These are all process-launch decisions, not background details.

12
00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.220
The working directory also matters.

13
00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:06.640
Relative paths used by the child are interpreted relative to its working directory.

14
00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:13.700
If the parent relies on a specific directory, it should set it explicitly or pass absolute paths where appropriate.

15
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:19.320
A service or automation wrapper should not accidentally decide this for the child.

16
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.200
Reviewers should ask what the child inherits and why.

17
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:29.300
If the launch uses the parent's environment and current directory unchanged, that should be an intentional choice.

18
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:35.960
If the child needs constrained behavior, build the environment and working directory as part of the launch contract.
